Research complete. Two approaches evaluated:

**Approach 1 (chosen) — BFS state-space search** over `(vol1, vol2)` states. Actions: fill/empty either bucket, pour either direction; prune the canonical forbidden state (start bucket empty AND other bucket full after an action); returns first state where either bucket == goal. BFS guarantees minimal moves, directly encodes the one subtle rule, returns exactly the required `(moves, goal_bucket, other_bucket)` tuple.
**Approach 2 (rejected) — deterministic pour-sequence / mathematical (Bézout)** — faster asymptotically but error-prone around the start-bucket constraint and much harder to prove correct against all canonical cases.

