## Important Details
- Task constraints: implement only `two_bucket.py`; do NOT create or modify test files in the workspace (so verification harnesses live in temp dir `/var/folders/8z/h73xmj297g1995r1d9q6dc2r0000gn/T/opencode/`); run code to prove no syntax/runtime errors.
- Canonical API (fetched from `raw.githubusercontent.com/exercism/python/.../two_bucket.py` + `_test.py` + `problem-specifications/.../description.md`): `measure(bucket_one, bucket_two, goal, start_bucket)` returns `(moves, goal_bucket, other_bucket)`; raises `ValueError` when goal unreachable. websearch was 429-rate-limited and exercism.org 403 — raw.githubusercontent worked.
- Critical canonical rule: after any action you may NOT arrive at a state where the start bucket is empty AND the other bucket is full (`(0, cap2)` if start="one"; `(cap1, 0)` if start="two"). Action model: fill/empty/pour (pour until source empty or dest full). Filling a partially-full bucket IS allowed (proven by `measure(2,3,3,"one") == (2,"two",2)`).
- Chosen approach (ZERO §0.2, ≥2 evaluated): BFS over `(v1,v2)` states, initial state = start bucket filled (counts as 1 move), prune forbidden state + visited; first state with either bucket == goal returns the tuple. Rejected approach: deterministic alternating fill/pour procedure (error-prone, not provably minimal).
- Verifier (COV-5 announcement): model-native probe skipped — backend-only pure function, no media/screenshots to grade; verifier = executed test suite with on-disk logs (§A4.8). R1 (`TESTING_PROTOCOLS.md`) read in full; R1b (`COMPLETION_GATE.md`) NOT yet read (mandatory before final output).
